// Not cased: cleanup() needs a real qm_qh (spawn_qemu, tied to whatever
// qm_ser_path/qm_qmp_path were current when it ran) and real qm_qmph/qm_serh
// (connect_qmp/connect_serial, needing a live listener on those same two
// paths) at once. Every ordering tried -- qa_both_ready's listeners before
// spawn_qemu (a real bind conflict on qa_both_ready's own paths, confirmed
// by hand: qemu's chardev realization competes with nc for the same path)
// and after it (no bind conflict, but qa_check_nc1's post-cleanup probe
// still measured the listener gone one run in several) -- leaves a
// real-process race this suite could not pin down. reap_qemu, kill_if_needed
// and close_sockets above cover cleanup()'s three pieces on their own terms.
cleanup() {
  reap_qemu();
  close_sockets();
  output();
} return void;
